rror": false, "num_turns": 5, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I fixed all 12 rules in `pricebook.py` whose behaviour didn't match their docstrings. A checker that compares each rule to its docstring over boundary quantities and a range of unit prices now finds 0 mismatches out of 150 rules.\n\nWhat was fixed:\n- **01**: the rule is marginal but discounted every unit. It now discounts only `(qty - 20)` units.\n- **06, 69, 71, 73, 149**: the threshold used `>` instead of `>=`, so the exact threshold quantity got no discount. Changed to `>=`.\n- **12**: the rate was 9% instead of 8%.\n- **20**: the rule is whole but was computed as marginal `(qty - 10)`. It now discounts every unit.\n- **24**: the 10,000-won cap only applied once the discount went over 20,000, so discounts between 10,000 and 20,000 weren't capped. The cap now always applies.\n- **53**: the threshold was 11 instead of 10.\n- **144**: the threshold was 6 instead of 5.\n- **147**: the 30,000 cap was applied to the price before the rate, not to the discount. It now caps the discount, as the module docstring says.\n\nNothing failed or was left unresolved. Rule 93 caps with an `if` statement instead of `min()`, but the result is the same, so I left it alone. The checker is in the scratchpad (`check.py`), not in the project.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 2258, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 34842, "uuid": "cfad9173-a786-4582-bd68-42af8d59d40d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1479, "time_to_request_ms": 370, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 8, "system_prompt": 12, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 12, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 0, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 1, "autocompact": 0, "query_setup": 1, "model_gates": 311, "tool_schema_build": 8, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 3, "request_build": 3}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time